{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters","id":989525,"title":"What are the toughest monsters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-18T14:04:01-07:00","id":989525,"title":"What are the toughest monsters?","content":"If I wanted to make a super-tanky supernatural, which splat would be the toughest? Just for health in general, no damage reduction or resistance/immunity to certain things. 2E releases, Beast and Demon only, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:12:28-07:00","id":989531,"title":"","content":"Werewolf is a perennial favorite for that, but if your goal is &quot;not dying no matter what&quot;, the best way to approach it is probably to make the sneakiest bastard ever, which ChroD gives you a lot of options for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:33:24-07:00","id":989541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=989531#post989531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf is a perennial favorite for that, but if your goal is &amp;quot;not dying no matter what&amp;quot;, the best way to approach it is probably to make the sneakiest bastard ever, which ChroD gives you a lot of options for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, but how do Prometheans fare in tankiness? They are high on my list of books to buy, with Werewolves being second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:41:10-07:00","id":989543,"title":"","content":"Every splat so far has ways to make pretty tough tanks. The questions are:<br /> <br /> 1a) Do you want tough mostly from innate powers, or tough from focused/purchased powers?<br /> 1b) If innate, are you looking at things everyone gets, or are specific sub-splats innate powers acceptable?<br /> 2) Do you prefer &quot;big numbers&quot; in the form of lots of Health and Armor, or more efficient use of the levels you have (like high end combat healing)?<br /> 3) How much does &quot;out of the gate&quot; vs. &quot;high end potential&quot; matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:45:13-07:00","id":989547,"title":"","content":"1.)No books, don't know.<br /> 2.) Big Health/Armor numbers. I know a pip equals 3 levels of damage, so a supernatural that can take up to full lethal before beginning to die.<br /> 3.)&quot;High End Potential&quot; is what I'm mostly after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:50:45-07:00","id":989553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=989547#post989547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.)No books, don't know.<br /> <b>2.) Big Health/Armor numbers. I know a pip equals 3 levels of damage, so a supernatural that can take up to full lethal before beginning to die.</b><br /> 3.)&quot;High End Potential&quot; is what I'm mostly after.</div> </div> </div> </div>I...don't understand this. All supernaturals can be full of lethal damage before starting to die. All everybody can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:58:25-07:00","id":989557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=989541#post989541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, but how do Prometheans fare in tankiness? They are high on my list of books to buy, with Werewolves being second.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheans are <i>really </i>tough. They don't go down until they hit full aggravated, and they don't suffer wound penalties. On top of that, they can spend pyros to eliminate damage as it happens, they can heal with electricity and if by some miracle you do manage to kill one they <i>come back to life</i> a few days later. Once. And then there's transmutations to consider...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:00:00-07:00","id":989559,"title":"","content":"I mean full lethal without penalty. Afaik, most everyone will begin to have a chance to pass out at full bashing, followed with chances to die at full lethal-aggravated damage. Prometheans can fight all the way full aggravated without dying","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:03:30-07:00","id":989560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=989559#post989559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean full lethal without penalty. Afaik, most everyone will begin to have a chance to pass out at full bashing, followed with chances to die at full lethal-aggravated damage. Prometheans can fight all the way full aggravated without dying</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they die once they reach full aggravated. But they can come back once (or as many times as they have body parts to sacrifice, in the case of some Osirians.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:04:27-07:00","id":989561,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, there's also a transmutation that lets prometheans hit full aggravated and <i>keep going. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:05:47-07:00","id":989562,"title":"","content":"Prometheans are pretty tough, because they ignore wound penalties and incapacitation from bashing/lethal damage. Basically, you have run them all the way to full Agg to put own down in a fight, and it takes a lot of non-Agg damage to slow them down. Werewolves probably have an edge due to combat healing, but if an Uratha can't risk going Gauru, a Promethean's innate endurance might overcome the werewolf's highers health and better healing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=989547#post989547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.)No books, don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is something you need the books for. It's an aesthetic choice. To give you some examples: Do you prefer a vampire that's greatest tanking is buying the Resilience Discipline, or a werewolf that's main toughness is that all werewolves can turn into the Gauru war form for a big boost to health and an insane boost to healing? Do you prefer something like Mage were all Mages get access to Mage Armor (though different forms that have different levels of basic toughness), or something like Changeling where most changelings don't get any significant boost to toughness, but some of the Kiths are extremely tough?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3.)&quot;High End Potential&quot; is what I'm mostly after. </div> </div> </div>Werewolf is probably a big contender here (esp. with some of the form boosting Merits) since werewolves start strong and have decent growth potential.<br /> <br /> Mages are always a contender for &quot;High End Potential&quot; because at their high end they're capable of extremely potent stuff; though they always come with the drawback of having to be prepared. Beating an Archmaster of Life is never going to be an easy fight though.<br /> <br /> Vampires probably fall a bit behind werewolves but have a nice balance of innate and growth potential. At high end a tank focused vampire is very scary though; and vampires have the advantage of free increases in Blood Potency over time, so they can focus XP towards specialties.<br /> <br /> Prometheans fall behind a bit on this because while very tough out of the gate, they don't grow that much compared to others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:10:02-07:00","id":989564,"title":"","content":"Prometheans and Uratha are absolute tanks. They can also regenerate from most wounds and have very specific weaknesses that your average PC can take advantage of.<br /> <br /> In terms of stuff that would just absolutely ruin your day however, low memory Mummies and Incarnate Beasts are nightmares to deal with. They have almost no weaknesses either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:13:17-07:00","id":989565,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, elder vamps have a trick where they can become totally invulnerable, but it costs 5 vitae a turn so they can only keep it up for so long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:23:06-07:00","id":989572,"title":"","content":"So, run around with an electric generator as a Promethean, then once the enemy gets me down kinda low, put the electric thing in my teeth, and turn the generator on for a little pick-me-up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:44:59-07:00","id":989580,"title":"","content":"Well, power lines and train tracks are more Iconic, but I guess that would work too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:47:14-07:00","id":989581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=989572#post989572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, run around with an electric generator as a Promethean, then once the enemy gets me down kinda low, put the electric thing in my teeth, and turn the generator on for a little pick-me-up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Should be fine, but those generators are heavy and hard to lug around even for a Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:57:53-07:00","id":989586,"title":"","content":"A vampire with Resilience is already a fairly tough one. Most damage sources will do only bashing by default even in the average vampire. Any source of damage that doesn't declare it keeps the damage cathegory in vampires, will be downgraded by any vampire. Then you get Resilience, and the first thing that happens is that the very few sources that cause Aggravated to the character now do so only with the damage that surpasses her Resilience value. And you also add Resilience to Health Levels.<br /> <br /> Then you start to use blood, this is reflexive. Your first default option to survive is to heal 2 Bashing or 1 Lethal with each Vitae. The second, and better, is to spend 1 Vitae to reduce the damage dealt by <u>each</u> source for a turn, equal Resilience for fire and banes, equal Resilience+1 for everything else.<br /> <br /> So you spend 1 Vitae with starting Resilience 3 whyle fighting an entire pack of werewolves, and each werewolf will deal 4 less damage if they hit, needing at least 5 damage just to scratch the vampire, and even then with a good chance of only dealing bashing damage (they can deal Lethal with bite or with a power that causes Aggravated. A power that causes Aggravated <u>and</u> declares that does such even to vampires, or that is fire-based, will cause Aggravated at the 4th HL of actual damage, that is, it have to cause at least 8 damage total, 7 if fire-based). Then you got to spend Vitae to heal any damage that happens to bypass this.<br /> <br /> If you get enough experience, after Resilience 5 you can either try Protean 3 to become a bear or something similar, or Vigor 3 to achieve Juggernaut's Gait, the costly Devotion of complete immunity, for when you really want to face something able to reliably dishe 10 or more fire-based damage per turn. With further investment in Celerity you get more all-purpose Defense, that will make successes on attack against you less likely to happen and potentialy less numerous, furthering survivability even more.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm not talking about specially lethal werewolves, just a casual battle against average ones. Nor am I saying that the vampire is the best tank you'll find. I'm just showing what a vampire can do, because I now it reasonably well. I would like to see similar work on other splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:02:47-07:00","id":989590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters#post989525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I wanted to make a super-tanky supernatural, which splat would be the toughest? Just for health in general, no damage reduction or resistance/immunity to certain things. 2E releases, Beast and Demon only, please.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You want best tank? Make a Wereelephant from the Changing Breeds book.<br /> <br /> I can't find the website, but somebody did a review of that book. Apparently a brand new Wereelephant straight out of character creation can destroy the world's greatest human with 5 in every physical skill / attribute.<br /> <br /> Apparently Changing Breeds had a lot of mechanical issues that weren't proof checked. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:07:50-07:00","id":989596,"title":"","content":"Chronicles of Darkness 2E releases, including Beast and Demon only, please. Changing Breeds is 1E","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:11:33-07:00","id":989597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=989596#post989596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chronicles of Darkness 2E releases, including Beast and Demon only, please. Changing Breeds is 1E</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well then for that, I'd have to say go with a Werewolf. I haven't checked out the second edition book, but from what I've heard, a Werewolf has the power to <i>completely heal itself within one round.</i> Unless the damage comes from something like silver, or whatever else Werewolves are vulnerable to.<br /> <br /> Unless your opponent was specifically prepared to fight a werewolf right then, the chances of them taking you down are pretty slim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:17:24-07:00","id":989600,"title":"","content":"High-Sekhem Mummies are an absolute nightmare, and are tanks even by supernatural standards. And as a bonus, it's extremely difficult to permanently kill them, probably harder than it is with any other 2e supernatural (no idea if Geist 2e will keep Sin-Eaters as overpowered as they were in 1e). I mean, Prometheans can come back, but Mummies can just keep doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:19:17-07:00","id":989603,"title":"","content":"I remember it being a little specific, but I'm not with the book right now and don't quite remember. But yes, I think any Gauru-form Uratha, or something like this, can heal everything you throw at it. But Gauru Form isn't somethin you can keep at will, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:23:15-07:00","id":989606,"title":"","content":"Werewolves in Gauru form heal all lethal and bashing damage every turn. Though it's worth noting that there are some drawbacks. You have a limited number of rounds to maintain it without having to change out, or fall into Death Rage; and generally speaking you only get to go Gauru once per fight (there are ways around that limit, but not enough to count on it every time for every character).<br /> <br /> In a &quot;white room&quot; the option of just falling to Rage isn't really that bad of a choice unless your enemy has Agg attacks.<br /> <br /> In a more &quot;real world&quot; scenario it becomes problematic. Even ignoring normal mortal witnesses, good tactics can do a lot. Rage means &quot;attack attack attack&quot; mode, and while not stupid, the attack mode means they can be lead into traps and such, leaving them open to big hits or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:27:43-07:00","id":989608,"title":"","content":"I think I'll make a Promethean tank, sounds like my kinda guy. If I'm lucky, I should be able to get Promethean and Werewolf, along with the others. Thanks for the advice and examples, I'll see about getting a game started here after Christmas, once I have books. Something on The Discord chat, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:31:57-07:00","id":989610,"title":"","content":"Rahu werewolves are especially hardy motherfuckers. They have access to the Full Moon Gift, which at purity 2+ lets them add said purity to their health. If they're also a blood talon that gives them an affinity for the Rage gift, which includes the werewolf version of resilience. At purity 5 they also get a neat power called Crimson Spasm, which lets them roll their purity + survival + stamina and divide successes however they like among their strength, stamina, armour or natural weapons for as long as they can afford to spend 1 essence per turn. And, as previously mentioned, in Gauru they regenerate all their non-aggravated wounds every turn, meaning to hurt them you need to do more than their health, which can easily be in the high teens, or use silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:47:46-07:00","id":989612,"title":"","content":"To explain how it works, it's actually a combination of several abilities. The base regeneration ability that all werewolves have is that every round they heal 1 Bashing, 15 minutes for 1 Lethal. They can spend Essence to turn that Bashing damage regen to restore Lethal instead. The amount they regen passively scales with Primal Urge. For every PU over 5, their regeneration becomes 1 point higher.<br /> <br /> They also remove all tilts as a result of damage whenever they heal an injury completely... so if they don't have anything marked in their boxes, they're at the pit of health with no maluses.<br /> <br /> Another aspect of the base regeneration is that it allows them to subtract the Toxicity of any poison or disease regardless of origin based on their PU on a 1:1 limit, so poison isn't going to cut it for some fights against the high level ones. I mean, RAW you could argue for them being in a torrent of mustard and cyanide gas and not be bothered.<br /> <br /> And lastly, they downgrade any Aggravated damage that is not from a supernatural source to Lethal. This includes things like fighting style effects, but may also extend to say... high explosives if you want to make that argument since explosives do Agg damage on a point blank attack.<br /> <br /> Combine these with Gauru healing every point of Lethal and Bashing every tun and you see why it's hard to put them down.<br /> In the right situation and without enough saturation fire to get them to roll over to aggravated, you can essentially have a character tank and walk off rocket launchers like it's nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mummies win my vote for just... keep coming back from the Dead Immortality though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 10-18-2016, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T17:03:59-07:00","id":989621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=989612#post989612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For every PU over 5, their regeneration becomes 1 point higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, actually it goes up to 2 per turn at 4 and 3 per turn at 6. Once you hit 7 the pattern does become 1+(PU-5) though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T19:53:04-07:00","id":989678,"title":"","content":"Beasts are pretty damn tanky if you put in the right Atavisms and Merits. The big ones are the Iron Skin merits, and the Atavisms Unbreakable, Looming Presence, and Relentless Hunter.<br /> <br /> I ran the numbers, and a Beast with the Unbreakable Atavism will, at Low (1-3) Satiety have 4/3 armor by default. Then if they have Stamina 4 they can take Iron Skin (advanced), which is a 1-2 dot merit that gives you armor against Lethal equal to its rating. So if you take that, they get 6/3 armor. If you then get to Stamina 5 they can take Iron Skin (epic) which removes the first level of damage from every attack they take, so that's functionally 7/3 armor there. If you also learn the Relentless Assault combat style up to 4 dots then you can have yet another point of armor when doing All-Out Attacks, so that's 8/3 armor. All of this will stack with actual mundane armor that you wear, so you can throw on some plate mail and be at 12/5 if you can get your hands on it. At Low Satiety they can't even wear you down with bashing damage if your armor reduces what you take to zero, you just don't take any damage.<br /> <br /> Then you spend a point of Satiety for Unbreakable and unarmed attacks and other natural sources of bashing damage stop hurting you, and lethal damage becomes bashing damage, for the scene, just to invalidate the small amount of damage you do take.<br /> <br /> If they have the Looming Presence Atavism then they add their Lair to their Size and Health. For a point of Satiety you can double this for the scene. It can also make you harder to hit in the first place by subtracting dice from your attacker's pool because they're so terrified of you.<br /> <br /> Relentless Hunter is for faster healing, so you start to look a bit more like a werewolf in that regard. It can also give you some resistance to poison and disease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T01:05:07-07:00","id":989768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=989678#post989678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts are pretty damn tanky if you put in the right Atavisms and Merits. The big ones are the Iron Skin merits, and the Atavisms Unbreakable, Looming Presence, and Relentless Hunter.<br /> <br /> I ran the numbers, and a Beast with the Unbreakable Atavism will, at Low (1-3) Satiety have 4/3 armor by default. Then if they have Stamina 4 they can take Iron Skin (advanced), which is a 1-2 dot merit that gives you armor against Lethal equal to its rating. So if you take that, they get 6/3 armor. If you then get to Stamina 5 they can take Iron Skin (epic) which removes the first level of damage from every attack they take, so that's functionally 7/3 armor there. If you also learn the Relentless Assault combat style up to 4 dots then you can have yet another point of armor when doing All-Out Attacks, so that's 8/3 armor. All of this will stack with actual mundane armor that you wear, so you can throw on some plate mail and be at 12/5 if you can get your hands on it. At Low Satiety they can't even wear you down with bashing damage if your armor reduces what you take to zero, you just don't take any damage.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just to add on that: Iron Skin gives Armor against Bashing equal to rating, Iron Skin (advanced) gives armor for <i>both </i>bashing and lethal. So you get + 2/0 with Iron Skin, and + 2/2 with Iron Skin (advanced) for a beautiful +4/2 in total. Just with low Satiety Unbreakable (or with spent Satiety on other Satiety Conditions) that's a pretty 8/5, butt naked. Add any bonuses from Styles of Armor, and you have a pretty tough Beast =D<br /> <br /> Btw, I love how there are so many ways to have a tank within CofD among different splats: We had explicit Beast, Vampire, Werewolf, Promethean and Mage &quot;builds&quot; so far. But what I am missing are Sin-Eaters. The ability to come back to life 4 times (5 with the initial one) and being unable to be knocked out should count for somthing, imho. Any players that could demonstrate how resilient the Bound (and maybe Changelings) are?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:25:46-07:00","id":989786,"title":"","content":"This is really interesting, and in ways that are hard to say what is the toughest one by default (in the high-end scenario). Distinct circumstances are going to favor distinct &quot;tank builds&quot;. But I don't know about Sin-Eaters and Changelings, I didn't read all the book on the former, nor saw anything about 2nd ed of the later. Going for 1st ed pattern and not looking in the books right now, I would suggest that Changelings probably get more from the Wyrd stat than most. If so, probably a High Wyrd Ogre will be very hard to fall, but it will be hard for a Changeling to go a long way without increasing Wyrd. But I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> I had one impression, though. It seems that werewolves are particularly lacking in ways around silver, whyle others can find stable ways around their personal banes. Am I right or did I miss something? Just for the record, the presented build for vampires does nothing against sunlight, but still works against any personal bane. And there are ways around sunlight with Coils of the Ascendant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:35:51-07:00","id":989792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=989768#post989768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what I am missing are Sin-Eaters. The ability to come back to life 4 times (5 with the initial one) and being unable to be knocked out should count for somthing, imho. Any players that could demonstrate how resilient the Bound (and maybe Changelings) are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Going off memory, in addition to not being knocked out and being able to resurrect over and over, they can create ridiculously tough armour around themselves through the shroud, can just decide to negate damage by spending plasm, can apply better of defense or wits to your defence, become immune to physical damage (though cannot manipulate objects) completely negate attacks that are after you in initiative, take bashing damage from firearms, immunity to being stunned, temporary health, spend plasm for increased defence, spend plasm to increase his finesse attribute and thus increase defense further, etc. But the bound aren't 2e so they aren't 100% on topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=989786#post989786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I don't know about Sin-Eaters and Changelings, I didn't read all the book on the former, nor saw anything about 2nd ed of the later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling have giant amounts of 2e content previewed actually on their section of the board. The introduction, chapter 1, chapter 3, section on Court Creation, section on the Hedge, section on Fetches and a section on Huntsmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-19-2016, 05:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:38:22-07:00","id":989793,"title":"","content":"Changeling 2E isn't actually out either, but we've seen enough of it that it basically is for our purposes. <br /> <br /> That said, Tankyness isn't exactly their thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:54:54-07:00","id":989803,"title":"","content":"As this is 2e only, I'll skip the Bound.<br /> <br /> From the 2e Changeling stuff (though this is somewhat subject to change):<br /> <br /> Earth Bones Ogre. Earth Bones gives you X/X armor equal to half your Wyrd, and you can spend glamour for more ballistic armor for a turn. And you don't suffer wound penalties.<br /> <br /> Grab the Potent Kith Merit (increases your Wyrd for calculating your armor by 1), Cloak of the Bear's Massive Form (Ogres can choose animals that are size 12, which is a huge boost to Health, on top of any boosts to Stamina appropriate), Cloak of the Elements 3 (3/3 armor that stacks with the Kith armor), Chrysalis (if your ST lets you stack it with with the previous two, which is a maybe in my mind, but if so 2/1 armor +1 Size for each success after the first).<br /> <br /> That package alone makes for an insanely tough customer.<br /> <br /> Tacking on Red Rage of Terrible Revenge is a bit of questionable choice for a tank, since it deals 1 lethal per turn to you, but you get a boost equal to your successes in Strength, Initiative, and general armor, as well as Wyrd/2 boost to Stamina that does boost Health for being an Ogre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:49:40-07:00","id":990260,"title":"","content":"If smaller splats are allowed then nothing in the Nwod/Chrod universe has anything on a Mask Slasher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11554-fate-inker","name":"Fate Inker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T22:53:30-07:00","id":990283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fate Inker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=990260#post990260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If smaller splats are allowed then nothing in the Nwod/Chrod universe has anything on a Mask Slasher.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why? I am not familiar with slashers (yet)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T23:54:38-07:00","id":990305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=990283#post990283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? I am not familiar with slashers (yet)</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC they only take a single point of damage (I think bashing maybe?) from any one attack, regardless of how much it would normally deal. So to fill them up with bashing you would have to hit them with a number of attacks equal to their health dots, and to fill them with Lethal you'd need to do so again, and a third time to kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T00:39:05-07:00","id":990319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=990305#post990305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC they only take a single point of damage (I think bashing maybe?) from any one attack, regardless of how much it would normally deal. So to fill them up with bashing you would have to hit them with a number of attacks equal to their health dots, and to fill them with Lethal you'd need to do so again, and a third time to kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, slashers are 1e and thus invalid. Also, demons get that ability (though you'd want really good medicine and wits to make it reliable (which isn't hard since this thread seems to assume high xp characters)), in addition to healing 1 hp per round, having armour for skin, able to spend it's fuel stat to reduce damage from aggravated to lethal or lethal to bashing, and being able to turn itself into a swarm that ensures survival as long as a single member of the swarm survives. So I don't see why just taking 1 damage each attack would make those slashers as the toughest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-20-2016, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:39:57-07:00","id":990337,"title":"","content":"Well, the ability lives on in the Horror dread powers. So there are things in ChroD who can do that, for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T09:39:56-07:00","id":990459,"title":"","content":"milo v3 raises a good point. We would need something like toughness per xp. Toughness being the sum of Regeneration, soak, defense, armor and life. Which seems like a huge hassle to calculate^^&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T09:59:12-07:00","id":990469,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sounds like quite a bit work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T10:31:44-07:00","id":990481,"title":"","content":"I think Werewolves definitely win on the regeneration front, closely followed by prometheans in power plants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T13:58:11-07:00","id":990615,"title":"","content":"And because werewolf regeneration is &quot;universal per character&quot;... they also win the price of effectiveness side of that debate too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T16:25:15-07:00","id":990678,"title":"","content":"Just for the sake of information, Mask Slashes don't reduce the damage cathegory, just the quantity to 1. It is fairly good on cot-effectiveness, since it costs nothing at all, and is awesome on the low-level games they're intended to be used. It is also a nasty surprise for PCs foccused on dealing damage. But for this thread's purpose, they're not really competitive on the long run. Without actual armor, those Slashers still suffer damage from any given hit as normal without much effort from the hitter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T17:20:29-07:00","id":990699,"title":"","content":"Dual kith Metalskin/Earthbones with Phantom Glory (elemental affinity fire), with 10 wyrd, is going to be tanky as hell, especially when embracing the wyrd which you can use to buff you defence by 10 per turn or 25 of you use all your per turn glamour to boost your defence.<br /> <br /> Also take cloak of the elements and Elemental Battle merit at 5 dots, so that immmersing yourself in the element you've become heals bashing damage.<br /> <br /> Oh and I forgot the name of the contract, but once per story you can go back in time, even if you died.<br /> <br /> Still using Embrace the Wyrd at Wyrd 10 makes you good at almost anything you choose.<br /> <br /> Take a frail, low strength flowering, have her embrace the wyrd at 10 wyrd and all of a sudden she can put her fist through a fucking brick wall one turn, defence tank the next, seduce someone else into helping her after that, do some ninji style back flips the turn after that, next turn do complex math and physics calculations that even stephen hawking would choke on, then the next turn apply the bonus dice to trick driving the get away car, while mooning the poor assholes whose butts she just kicked so maybe Embrace the Wyrd shouldn't count ;p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 10-20-2016, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T18:32:36-07:00","id":990735,"title":"","content":"It's obviously top-end stuff, but a Purity 5 Rahu werewolf has a technically uncapped potential number of health levels due to exploding 10s on the Crimson Spasm activation roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T18:50:12-07:00","id":990745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=990735#post990735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's obviously top-end stuff, but a Purity 5 Rahu werewolf has a technically uncapped potential number of health levels due to exploding 10s on the Crimson Spasm activation roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Acanthus/Rahu teamup strikes me as terrifying with this in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T18:55:44-07:00","id":990746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=990745#post990745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Acanthus/Rahu teamup strikes me as terrifying with this in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, the question you have to ask yourself is, how long would they be able to put up with each other? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T19:01:01-07:00","id":990748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=990746#post990746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, the question you have to ask yourself is, how long would they be able to put up with each other? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>'At'd depend on the people. I can imagine pairings that would kill each other and pairings that would be best buds.<br /> <br /> I imagine the dialogue, either way, would involve a lot of back and forth escalation/de-escalation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steel