he amount of, 'This seems a little overpowered,' if you tagged a, 'If the Uratha is in Basu-Im, it costs no Essence to use and it will be used instinctively,' onto it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T23:53:03-07:00","id":990827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpiritSponge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters?p=990752#post990752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a demon with armored plates, plasma drive and aegis protocol. Then top it off with an exploit like break to heal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget the embed that reduces damage of each attack to 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T07:11:14-08:00","id":1045042,"title":"","content":"Just to bring up how cool Unbreakable is for Beasts again: Upon spending Satiety, the Beast reduces all sources of Bashing into nothingness, lethal to bashing, and his armor applies to Agg Dmg.<br /> Spending Satiety on Relentless Hunter allows the Beast to heal [Lair] dots of Agg or all lethal and all bashing damage, and for the rest of the scene cannot be stunned or incapacitated, and does not suffer injury-related penalties. Kind of a Promethean mode, so to speak. Furthermore, a Low Satiety Beast with Relentless Hunter can downgrade damage equal to 2x[Lair] after a scene, with Agg to Lethal, Lethal to Bashing and/or Bashing into nothingness.<br /> Both together make a pretty great combination (adding Looming Presence just makes them even more tanky + gives something like a bonus on Defense).<br /> Those two are pretty tanky AND pretty cost efficient. Not the tankiest there is, but pretty tanky.<br /> <br /> Taking the Iron Skin, Giant and Iron Skin advanced Merits, Looming Presence and Unbreakable, you can have a Beast with 7/5 (8/6 when hungry) Armor and 11 HP (12 upon spending Satiety) at creation when focusing on tankiness. That's a good start, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:55:17-08:00","id":1045321,"title":"","content":"People seem to be selling Vampires short. They can be <i>obscene</i> tanks in a way that doesn't make them obviously inhuman - heck, the Ordo Dracul can do so <i>really</i> cheaply (from a Vitae perspective). Observe!<br /> <br /> 0) Kindred downgrade most damage they take by one step. In other words, most sources are going to be hitting them with Bashing <i>to start with</i>.<br /> 1) Resilience is <i>really good</i> as a starting point. Each dot gives you +1 Stamina and reduces a level of Aggravated from non-sunlight sources to Lethal.<br /> 2) For 1 vitae a scene, <a href=\"http://pastebin.com/XPbSdVS4\" target=\"_blank\">.22 Solid</a> makes each dot of Resilience <i>also</i> reduce a level of Lethal damage to Bashing.<br /> 3) Coil of the Ascendant 4 makes fire deal Lethal damage if you've got the Blush of Life active (which costs you 1 vitae per 24 hours), and makes each dot of Resilience reduce one level of that damage to Bashing.<br /> 4) Rite of the Impaled 2 turns all of your Wound Penalties into bonuses, <i>and</i> ensures that you don't fall into Torpor until you have suffered [Resolve] Aggravated health levels worth of damage.<br /> <br /> In total, for <i>1 Vitae a scene</i>, the first five damage you take from <i>any</i> source is Bashing. If it's fire-based, the first <i>ten</i> levels are Bashing. You can spend 1 Vitae to subtract the first 6 levels of damage from non-Bane sources, which applies <i>before</i> you downgrade damage. You can spend another Vitae to subtract the first 5 levels of damage from non-Sunlight banes as well.<br /> <br /> This all costs 26xp if you start off as a Gangrel with CotA 1/Protean 1/Resilience 1 and Rite of the Impaled 2. You still have 6 merit dots to play with (you need Status (Ordo Dracul 1) and Sworn to take Rite of the Impaled), and you can get to .22 Solid in 5xp, CotA 4 in 9xp, and Resilience 5 in 12xp.<br /> <br /> Remember, too, that Vampires have a couple of sources of <i>cheap</i> power - Diablerie and the Vow of Matrimony come to mind.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> Moving away from Major Templates (thanks Hurt Locker!)<br /> <br /> 1) Plain jane mortals can pick up Telekinesis 5 and Telekinetic Dodge for 8xp, which adds +5 successes to a Dodge for 1wp. That's enough to turn an exceptional success into a failure, for reference.<br /> <br /> 2) Atariya are <i>obscenely</i> hard to kill. Damn Lucky lets you redirect a little bit of damage each scene, and Nine Lives lets you survive <i>anything</i> up to five times.<br /> <br /> 3) The Infected can get [Stamina/Stamina] armor (Bulletman Syndrome) and rapid regeneration (The New Flesh lets you heal Aggravated at the same speed as Lethal).<br /> <br /> 4) The Lost Boys can get nice Stamina boosts (Augmented Resilience 3 gives you +3 Stamina and <i>sometimes</i> gives you 2/1 Armor), and can pick up occasional 3/3 Armor for 4xp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 02-07-2017, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:58:53-08:00","id":1045322,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, I forgot:<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul also have the Coil of Zirnitra, which lets you pick up Supernatural merits. So your Stamina 15 Elder could pick up Bulletman Syndrome and could abuse the fact that they now have 15/15 Armor <i>all the time</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:44:25-08:00","id":1045402,"title":"","content":"As it concerns ultimate high-end potential, mages (as usual) get unbeatable. Archmasters are one Imperial spell with indefinite duration away from immortality as complete as it can get this side of Ascension, since &quot;I cannot die, ever&quot; is a typical application of the Practices of Entities and Excision (Imperial Mysteries quotes it as an option for Death and Life).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 02-07-2017, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:57:22-08:00","id":1045410,"title":"","content":"I hope they add a vast series of, 'I will not be tormented by ceaseless agony as I'm torn apart over and over, driven to gibbering madness, wishing to end my existence but unable to muster the power to do so, ever.'<br /> <br /> Anyways,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989525-what-are-the-toughest-monsters#post989525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I wanted to make a super-tanky supernatural, which splat would be the toughest? Just for health in general, no damage reduction or resistance/immunity to certain things. 2E releases, Beast and Demon only, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine we're taking into account Promethean and Mage now that they're second edition, but immunity and damage reduction is still off limits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-07-2017, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T18:02:11-08:00","id":1045531,"title":"","content":"<i>Technically</i> an Ordo Dracul member with the Coil of Zirnitra and enough surgery (<i>so</i> much surgery) can pull off <i>all</i> of these tank powers.<br /> <br /> Oh Grafting Unholy Flesh, I disagree with your existence <i>so hard</i>...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],